The change swaps `viewsets.ModelViewSet` for `viewsets.ReadOnlyModelViewSet` on `MemoryViewSet`, which removes the create/update/partial-update endpoints. This is a reduction of exposed write operations, not an addition. The retained read path (`get_queryset`) enforces `memory.manage`, and the retained `destroy` enforces `memory.delete` via `perm_check`. The change does not introduce or newly expose any authorization weakness; the only pre-existing oddity (a non-raising `permission_denied` in `get_queryset`) is in unchanged code and is not newly exposed by this PR.

